[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
Beryllium is a development build (Phase 1).

Sandbox status: none. Like www/chromium today, no Beryllium process runs in
Capsicum capability mode yet. Do not rely on this release to contain a
compromised web page. The sandbox status of each release is published at
https://github.com/johnjanik/Beryllium.

- Updates arrive through pkg (pkg upgrade); there is no in-browser updater.
- Profile: ~/.config/beryllium (override with BERYLLIUM_CONFIG_HOME).
- Policies: %%PREFIX%%/etc/beryllium/policies/managed/
- Wayland is recommended. Under X11, any program in the session can read
  input from and inject input into other windows.
- Helium services (extension proxy, !bangs list, filter-list and component
  updates, dictionaries) are off by default; see the project documentation
  for what that changes.
- Optional system hardening that blocks some cross-process observation:
    sysctl security.bsd.see_other_uids=0
    sysctl security.bsd.see_other_gids=0
    sysctl security.bsd.unprivileged_proc_debug=0   (also stops users
      debugging their own programs)
- kern.ipc.shm_allow_removed=1 is required (the launcher checks it).
EOM
}
]
